menu "BreezyBox"

    config BREEZYBOX_SHELL_SCRIPTING
        bool "Enable rich shell scripting (POSIX-ish subset)"
        default n
        help
            Enable the BreezyBox shell script interpreter: quoting, parameter
            expansion, command substitution, arithmetic, globbing, control
            flow (if/while/for/case, functions), test/[, && and ||,
            redirection, here-docs, and temp-file pipes.

            When enabled, `sh <file>` and the init script are run through the
            new interpreter (reading the whole file into a buffer), and the
            interactive prompt keeps its per-line dispatch for simple commands.

            When disabled (the default), behavior is byte-for-byte the current
            line-at-a-time runner and no extra code or SRAM is used. Leave this
            off on SRAM-constrained targets that do not need scripting.

endmenu
